  "key_static_findings": [
    "PQ-HSA device-backed paged serving retains full engine KV and adds index; core API separately exposes CPU/offload.",
    "PQ-HSA batch runtime creates per-request sidecars, digest uses full prompt, and loops request replay; optional within-layer codebook sharing exists.",
    "PQ-HSA fast paged CUDA explicitly reads at::Half; BF16 direct use is not qualified.",
    "PQ-HSA default architecture is 9.0, while is_hopper accepts major>=9; neither proves SM120 compatibility.",
    "PQ-HSA TP worker entry and TP launcher knob exist; V2 request-state adapter explicitly not ported; target 0.31 V2/FP8 weights/BF16 KV/TP2 is unqualified.",
    "PQ-HSA default periodic batched deferred flush includes EMA, full retrieval gather in paged mode, whole list-id sorting, and possible graph invalidation.",
    "HiSparse current pinned validator excludes ordinary Qwen GQA and requires radix cache disabled; pinned docs require PD mode and describe SM120 GLM DSA FP8 support.",
    "Both are prior art constraints; this review establishes no new algorithm, quality recovery, capacity release, or speedup on this project."
  ],
